msgid "Work live with EM Tools in Blender"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Keep EMStudio and EM Tools in Blender on the same graph and the same "
"selection.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"EM Tools is the add-on of the Extended Matrix for Blender. When EMStudio "
"works live with it, the two programs look at the same graph: a unit "
"selected in EMStudio is selected in Blender, an object selected in "
"Blender is selected in EMStudio, and Blender can model a proxy for a unit"
" on request. The em.json stays the reference of the study; the live link "
"is a convenience between two programs on the same computer, or on the "
"same network."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the section **Where you work** of the chip's menu (the chip at the top"
" right of the window) this way of working is called **With an app**. The "
"older versions called it *Sidecar*."
msgstr ""

msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Install Blender and EM Tools, and open in Blender the study you want to "
"work on, with its graph loaded in the EM panel. In Templu Mare, the graph"
" *Temple*."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In Blender, in the tab **EM ▸ Where you work**, press **Work with "
"EMStudio**. EM Tools then keeps a connection open, and EMStudio connects "
"to it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The address EMStudio uses is in ``Settings… ▸ Connections``, section "
"**Synchronised apps**: **Sync with** is **Blender · EMtools**, and "
"**Protocol**, **Host / IP** and **Port** compose the **Address** shown "
"underneath (see :doc:`/reference/settings`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Connect EMStudio to Blender"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Click the label at the left of the status bar, or press :kbd:`⇧⌘L` "
"(:kbd:`Ctrl+Shift+L` on Windows and Linux). The chip's menu opens at the "
"section **Where you work**."
msgstr ""

msgid "Under **Mode**, choose **With an app**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Under **Synchronised apps**, the line of Blender says **connected**. If "
"it says **waiting for it**, EMStudio has not found Blender yet: it asks "
"again every three seconds by itself. Press **Find** to try the ports EM "
"Tools uses on this computer; when one answers, EMStudio says **found at**"
" with its address and keeps that address in the settings. If the line "
"still waits, choose **On this computer** and then **With an app** again: "
"the new connection uses the address found."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Blender sends its graph. The graph becomes the active one in EMStudio, "
"and its name is followed by **from Blender (sync)** in the list of "
"graphs, in the title and in the name strip. A line in the Log says that "
"the active graph is now Blender's graph, live, and not the file's."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If no graph is loaded in Blender, EMStudio says so and names the graphs "
"Blender lists. Load the graph from the EM panel in Blender: it arrives in"
" EMStudio by itself, with no new connection."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the graph in Blender is written with another version of the Extended "
"Matrix datamodel than the file open in EMStudio, a message names the two "
"versions."
msgstr ""

msgid "Work with the two programs"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Selection.** Select a unit in the Matrix, in the **Outliner** or in the"
" Space: Blender selects its proxy. Select an object in Blender: EMStudio "
"selects its node, and **Zoom to selection** frames it when that switch is"
" on. Several objects selected in Blender arrive as a multiple selection."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**What arrives from Blender.** When the mode is **With an app**, the "
"section **Where you work** shows **What you accept from Blender**, with "
"three choices: **Everything** (the selection and the changes to the "
"graph, the default), **Selection only**, and **Nothing**. What you choose"
" applies to this window; what EMStudio sends always leaves, and Blender "
"decides what it takes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**A proxy modelled in Blender.** Select a unit. In the **Inspector**, "
"section **Proxy**, press **Model the proxy in Blender**. Blender makes a "
"box at its 3D cursor, named after the unit, in its *Proxy* collection, "
"and its geometry comes back into the graph as a property of the unit. A "
"proxy already in Blender's scene is selected there instead, and nothing "
"is added."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**A resource imported in Blender.** On a resource, the **Inspector** "
"offers **Import geometry in Blender**: Blender imports its mesh, and what"
" it creates comes back into the graph."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**A node shown in Blender.** In the **Inspector**, section **Open "
"with…**, **Blender / EMtools · select it** selects the node's object in "
"Blender."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The two commands that ask Blender to model need its consent. If the "
"button is greyed out, its tooltip says why: either EMStudio is not "
"connected, or, in Blender, the tab **EM ▸ Where you work ▸ Permissions…**"
" does not have **EMStudio may model in this scene** ticked."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When the two programs have different documents open, EMStudio says so in "
"the Log and in the panel, with **different doc** beside the app: working "
"on two documents is allowed, and it is the reason why a selection finds "
"nothing on the other side."
msgstr ""

msgid "Open a .blend in Blender from EMStudio"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the **Archive** workspace, in the **Files** window, right-click a "
"``.blend`` file."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Choose **Open in Blender**. EMStudio starts the Blender of this computer "
"on that file, joined to the open graph through the same live link."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The same menu offers **Open as a folder**, which lists the objects of the"
" ``.blend`` inside the **Files** window. There, **Selection synchronised "
"with Blender** makes a click on an object select it in Blender, and a "
"selection in Blender pick the matching objects in the list. The other "
"commands of that view are described in :doc:`compose-a-blend`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Stop working live"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the section **Where you work** of the chip's menu, under **Mode**, "
"choose **On this computer**. EMStudio stops waiting for Blender, or "
"closes the link, and the graph that came from Blender leaves the list: it"
" belongs to Blender. The file you had open stays open, as it was."
msgstr ""

msgid "What you get"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"One study seen by two programs: the stratigraphy in EMStudio, the 3D in "
"Blender, with the selection shared, the proxies modelled in Blender and "
"returned to the graph, and every change that you accept from Blender "
"recorded in the graph like any other change."
msgstr ""

msgid "See also"
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`compose-a-blend`, to prepare a working ``.blend`` from the graph."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`/how-to/space/place-objects`, to place the models in EMStudio's own"
" Space."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`/reference/settings`, section *Connections*, for the address of the"
" link."
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`/reference/inspector`, sections *Proxy* and *Open with…*."
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`/explanation/open-enter-create`, for the three ways of working."
msgstr ""

